goto routines_intro_exit

remstart
    THE FIRST DIVE
    the very first game is a little tutorial. the wave of bubbles goes by and there is nothing there
    but the water. a few lines of text go by, one at a time:

        This is a match 3 game.
        Take your time.
        Soak it in.

    the confirm button skips the lines.

    THE LITTLE BOARDS
    players did not see that the cursor can go anywhere without it costing anything, or that a group
    of fish does not have to be in a straight line. so the game starts on a board of three by three,
    and grows, a ring at a time, with one thing to learn on each:

        3 by 3      a seahorse, a crab and a seahorse in a row, with one more seahorse under the
                    crab. the cursor is on the crab. "Hold [swap] and push [dir] to swap."
                    the pop brings in the count of moves, and the multiplier.
        5 by 5      the next match is up in the far corner, away from the cursor.
                    "You can move around for free." the count of moves does not go up on the way.
                    under the board: "A swap that pops nothing costs multiplier."
        7 by 7      the only match is a group in the shape of an L.
                    "Fish do not need to be in straight lines."

    a little board keeps the cells the size that they are on the board that the game starts with, and
    it sits in the middle of where that board will be. so a fish of one little board is still in the
    same spot on the screen on the next one, and the new fish grow in around it. the fish are laid out
    by hand, in tutorialLayoutKind. any swap can be made. on the second board, the swap that the board
    is about is the only one that pops anything, so every other swap there costs the multiplier, the
    way it does in the game: the line under the board comes back, and the bar wiggles. on the first
    and third boards, a few other swaps pop too, and that is fine.
    any pop brings in the next board. the fish that drop in after a pop are the ones that the next
    board has there, so after the swap that the board is about, nothing changes when it grows. after
    some other pop, the fish that are not what the next board has there grow in again as the right
    ones. a test in fish_tests_tutorial plays every board, to check all of that.

    the third pop fades the little board away, and the things around it, which leaves the water. the
    line about info mode comes up, and the hint for it is the only hint, brighter than usual. it waits
    for the key, and starts to bob after a few seconds. the key brings in the whole board, and info
    mode opens over it. it is the board that the game was dealt before the tutorial started, with its
    streams of the seed where they were, and the moves and the multiplier go back to how a game
    starts. so a seed plays the same game, with the tutorial or without it. the bar of the round and
    the rounds that are left come in with it.

    THE FISH OF THE MYSTERY
    when info mode is closed, the board fades away to the water, and one seahorse shows up. now and
    then a question mark comes up out of it. it turns around and back, rolls belly up and back,
    shimmers with the rainbow, and swaps out to the left, into nothing, and back. "Remember," is over
    the fish, and "The ocean is mysterious." under it. then a screen of its own: "You cannot lose.",
    with "Get through 30 rounds in as few moves as possible." under it. then the board comes back.
    that is the end of the tutorial.

    THE FIRST UPGRADE
    when the first round of a game that had the tutorial is won, the board fades away again before the
    upgrade screen comes up, no bubbles float up, and a few lines go by: "Hi again.", "You finished the
    first round." with "Good job!" under it, and "Now you may select an upgrade."

    a piece that has not come in yet is not explained in info mode, and it does not count anything
    yet either. no moves are counted, and the multiplier does not fill, until they can be seen, and
    nothing scores until the bar can be seen. tutorialMovesOff() and tutorialScoreOff(), in
    fish_funcs, are how the rest of the game asks. the game is not saved until the tutorial is over.

    TUTORIAL_STAGE says how far along it is. it is 0 when there is no tutorial, which is nearly always,
    and then nothing here does anything.

    it happens by itself once: PREF_INTRO_SEEN remembers which INTRO_VERSION was seen, with the
    options. raising INTRO_VERSION shows a new tutorial to everyone, once. after that, the page that
    "New Game" opens has a line to ask for it again. see OPTION_GAME_INTRO.
    setting the FISH_INTRO environment variable asks for it every time, to look at it.

    the rest of the game does these things for it:
    - reset_game ends a tutorial that was going, with tutorial_end
    - starting a new game calls tutorial_prepare before the wave of bubbles, and run_first_dive_intro after it
    - handle_combos calls tutorial_pop when a move pops fish, and gives the new fish of a little board
      from tutorialNewFish
    - the main loop calls tutorial_advance, which brings in the next board once the pops have settled
    - startLiveMove asks tutorialBlocksSwap about every swap
    - judgeMultiplierSwaps calls tutorialMissed when a swap pops nothing
    - handle_ability_selection calls tutorial_upgrade_talk before the first upgrade screen

    THE HINTS
    this part is nothing to do with the tutorial, and it is always on. the line of key hints along the
    bottom of the game is three texts side by side: one for moving, one for swapping, and one for
    info mode. each one gives a little shake when the player does the thing that it is about, and
    the other two stay still. frame_hints lays them out and shakes them, and update_frame comes to it.

    every other screen writes its own hints on the one text that was always there, INFO_HINT_TEXT_ID.
    so the three are only shown while the game is what is being played. the screens say so with
    hintMode(), and the menu puts all of the hints away and brings them back with hintShow().
remend

setup_intro:
    ` the globals are declared in the fish headers

    ` the water goes a little darker behind the lines, so that they can be read
    reserve sprite id(INTRO_DIM_SPRITE)
    sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, 0, 0, TEX_PIXEL
    set sprite offset INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, 0, 0
    size sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, WORLD_WIDTH, WORLD_HEIGHT
    color sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, rgb(4, 8, 24, 0)
    order sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, ORDER_INTRO
    hide sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE

    ` at this size, the picture of a key in a line is exactly twice as big as it was drawn
    reserve text id(INTRO_TEXT_ID)
    text INTRO_TEXT_ID, WORLD_WIDTH / 2, WORLD_HEIGHT / 2, SCORE_FONT, " "
    size text max INTRO_TEXT_ID, WORLD_WIDTH - 40, 32 `a long line shrinks to fit across the screen
    set text offset INTRO_TEXT_ID, .5, .5
    color text INTRO_TEXT_ID, rgb(255, 255, 255, 0)
    ` a few orders over the dark, because the engine breaks a tie of order by id, and the dark was made later
    order text INTRO_TEXT_ID, ORDER_INTRO + 4
    enable rich text INTRO_TEXT_ID `so that a line can show a picture of a key, like {info}
    hide text INTRO_TEXT_ID

    ` the words over a little board. frame_hints puts them just above its top row, and fades them.
    reserve text id(TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID)
    text TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID, WORLD_WIDTH / 2, WORLD_HEIGHT / 2, SCORE_FONT, " "
    size text max TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID, 340, 32 `between the moves on the left of the board and the rounds on the right
    set text offset TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID, .5, 1
    color text TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID, rgb(255, 255, 255, 255)
    order text TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID, ORDER_INTRO + 4
    enable rich text TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID `so that it can show a picture of a key, like {swap}
    enable text drop shadow TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID, 2, -2, rgb(0,0,0)
    set text alpha TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID, 0
    hide text TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID
    reserve tween id(TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TWEEN_ID)
    create basic tween TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TWEEN_ID, 0, 0, 1, 0

    ` the line under a little board, about a swap that pops nothing. it is the color of the multiplier's
    ` "no", and the size of the hints, so that their pictures of keys are as sharp as the hints' are.
    reserve text id(TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID)
    text loc TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID, WORLD_WIDTH / 2, WORLD_HEIGHT / 2, SCORE_FONT, "intro.tut.miss"
    size text max TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID, 340, 16
    set text offset TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID, .5, 0
    color text TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID, rgb(255, 230, 150, 255)
    order text TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID, ORDER_INTRO + 4
    enable text drop shadow TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID, 2, -2, rgb(0,0,0)
    set text alpha TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID, 0
    hide text TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID
    reserve tween id(TUTORIAL_SUB_TWEEN_ID)
    create basic tween TUTORIAL_SUB_TWEEN_ID, 0, 0, 1, 0

    ` the smaller line under a line of tutorial_lines, like "Good job!"
    reserve text id(INTRO_SUB_TEXT_ID)
    text loc INTRO_SUB_TEXT_ID, WORLD_WIDTH / 2, WORLD_HEIGHT / 2 + 24, SCORE_FONT, "intro.line.goodjob"
    size text max INTRO_SUB_TEXT_ID, WORLD_WIDTH - 40, 16
    set text offset INTRO_SUB_TEXT_ID, .5, 0
    color text INTRO_SUB_TEXT_ID, rgb(255, 230, 150, 0)
    order text INTRO_SUB_TEXT_ID, ORDER_INTRO + 4
    enable text drop shadow INTRO_SUB_TEXT_ID, 2, -2, rgb(0,0,0)
    hide text INTRO_SUB_TEXT_ID

    ` the lines under the bar of the round, and the outline around it. see tutorial_round_bar.
    reserve text id(TUTORIAL_BAR_TEXT_ID)
    text loc TUTORIAL_BAR_TEXT_ID, WORLD_WIDTH / 2, 60, SCORE_FONT, "intro.tut.bar"
    size text max TUTORIAL_BAR_TEXT_ID, 400, 20
    set text offset TUTORIAL_BAR_TEXT_ID, .5, 0
    color text TUTORIAL_BAR_TEXT_ID, rgb(255, 255, 255, 255)
    order text TUTORIAL_BAR_TEXT_ID, ORDER_INTRO + 4
    enable text drop shadow TUTORIAL_BAR_TEXT_ID, 2, -2, rgb(0,0,0)
    hide text TUTORIAL_BAR_TEXT_ID
    reserve text id(TUTORIAL_BAR_SUB_TEXT_ID)
    text loc TUTORIAL_BAR_SUB_TEXT_ID, WORLD_WIDTH / 2, 84, SCORE_FONT, "intro.tut.bar.sub"
    size text max TUTORIAL_BAR_SUB_TEXT_ID, 400, 16
    set text offset TUTORIAL_BAR_SUB_TEXT_ID, .5, 0
    color text TUTORIAL_BAR_SUB_TEXT_ID, rgb(255, 230, 150, 255)
    order text TUTORIAL_BAR_SUB_TEXT_ID, ORDER_INTRO + 4
    enable text drop shadow TUTORIAL_BAR_SUB_TEXT_ID, 2, -2, rgb(0,0,0)
    hide text TUTORIAL_BAR_SUB_TEXT_ID
    TUTORIAL_BAR_BORDER = createInfoBorder(ORDER_INTRO + 3)

    ` the question marks of the mystery. a question mark is not a word, so it is the same in every language.
    for markI = 0 to TUTORIAL_MARK_COUNT - 1
        reserve text id(TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI))
        text TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI), 0, 0, SCORE_FONT, "?"
        size text y TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI), 16
        set text offset TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI), .5, .5
        color text TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI), rgb(170, 210, 255, 255)
        order text TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI), ORDER_INTRO + 2
        set text alpha TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI), 0
        hide text TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(markI)
        TUTORIAL_MARK_BORN(markI) = 0
    next

    ` the kinds of fish that the rows of the little boards are written in. see tutorialLayoutKind.
    TUTORIAL_KINDS(1) = TEX_PUFFER
    TUTORIAL_KINDS(2) = TEX_CATFISH
    TUTORIAL_KINDS(3) = TEX_GOLDFISH
    TUTORIAL_KINDS(4) = TEX_ANGELFISH
    TUTORIAL_KINDS(5) = TEX_CRAB
    TUTORIAL_KINDS(6) = TEX_BASS `the seahorse. see fish_routines_customart.
    TUTORIAL_KINDS(7) = TEX_WORM `the starfish

    ` the three key hints of the game. they look the same as the text that the other screens write theirs on.
    for hintI = 0 to 2
        reserve text id(HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI))
        text HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI), 0, WORLD_HEIGHT - 2, SCORE_FONT, " "
        order text HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI), ORDER_HUD_TEXT
        enable rich text HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI)
        set text offset HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI), 0, 1
        size text y HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI), 16
        color text HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI), rgb(64, 128, 255, 140)
        HINT_PART_ALPHA#(hintI) = HINT_PART_SHOWN_ALPHA
        enable text drop shadow HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI), 2, -2, rgb(0,0,0)

        reserve tween id(HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(hintI))
        create basic tween HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(hintI), 0, 0, 1, 0
    next
    set text loc HINT_PART_TEXTS(0), "intro.hint.move"
    set text loc HINT_PART_TEXTS(1), "intro.hint.swap"
    set text loc HINT_PART_TEXTS(2), "intro.hint.info"

    ` the jumps of the pictures of keys in the words of the tutorial. see ICON_PUNCH_TWEENS in fish_headers.
    ` the ids are the ones that frame_input_icons gives them, whatever is being played with.
    ICON_PUNCH_IDS(0) = 6 `{swap}
    ICON_PUNCH_IDS(1) = 7 `{dir}
    ICON_PUNCH_IDS(2) = 5 `{info}
    for iconI = 0 to 2
        reserve tween id(ICON_PUNCH_TWEENS(iconI))
        create basic tween ICON_PUNCH_TWEENS(iconI), 0, 0, 1, 0
    next
return


` a new game is about to start. if it is the first one, or the intro was asked for, take everything
` off of the screen, so that the wave of bubbles uncovers nothing but the water.
tutorial_prepare:
    tutWanted = 0
    tutSeen = get pref(PREF_INTRO_SEEN, 0)
    if tutSeen < INTRO_VERSION then tutWanted = 1
    if OPTION_GAME_INTRO then tutWanted = 1
    if is env set("FISH_INTRO") then tutWanted = 1

    ` it has to be asked for again every time
    OPTION_GAME_INTRO = 0

    if tutWanted = 0 then return
    set pref PREF_INTRO_SEEN, INTRO_VERSION
    TUTORIAL_STAGE = 1
    TUTORIAL_UPGRADE_TALK = 1 `a few words before the first upgrade screen too. see tutorial_upgrade_talk.
    TUTORIAL_SCORE_HOLD = 0
    TUTORIAL_BOARD = 0
    TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE = 0

    ` the game has been dealt its board already. it is kept for when the little boards are done, along
    ` with the way the fish face, and where the streams of the seed had got to, so that the tutorial does
    ` not change what the seed plays. see THE LITTLE BOARDS, at the top of this file.
    for tutI = 0 to CELL_COUNT - 1
        TUTORIAL_DEAL(tutI) = CELLS(tutI).value
        hide sprite CELLS(tutI).spriteId
    next
    for tutI = 0 to 399
        TUTORIAL_DEAL_FACE(tutI) = SCHOOL_FACE(tutI)
    next
    TUTORIAL_DEAL_SPAWNS = SCHOOL_SPAWNS
    for tutI = 0 to 2
        TUTORIAL_RNG(tutI * 2) = random stream state(tutI, 0)
        TUTORIAL_RNG(tutI * 2 + 1) = random stream state(tutI, 1)
    next
    hide sprite SELECTION_SPRITE
    hintShow(0)

    gosub tutorial_hide_moves
    gosub tutorial_hide_score

return


` the lines of text, and then the first of the little boards. a new game comes here when the wave of
` bubbles has gone.
run_first_dive_intro:
    if TUTORIAL_STAGE <> 1 then return

    introFade# = INTRO_FADE_MS
    introCount = 3 `how many lines there are
    introTotal = INTRO_LINE_MS * introCount
    introStart = game ms()
    introShown = -1
    introDone = 0

    show sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE
    show text INTRO_TEXT_ID

    while introDone = 0
        introAge = game ms() - introStart

        ` which line is up
        introLine = 0
        if introAge >= INTRO_LINE_MS then introLine = 1
        if introAge >= INTRO_LINE_MS * 2 then introLine = 2
        if introAge >= introTotal then introLine = introCount

        if introLine >= introCount
            introDone = 1
        else
            if introLine <> introShown
                introShown = introLine
                if introLine = 0 then set text loc INTRO_TEXT_ID, "intro.line.match3"
                if introLine = 1 then set text loc INTRO_TEXT_ID, "intro.line.time"
                if introLine = 2 then set text loc INTRO_TEXT_ID, "intro.line.soak"
            endif

            ` every line fades in, stays a while, and fades out
            introLineStart = introLine * INTRO_LINE_MS
            introIn# = introAge - introLineStart
            introLeft# = INTRO_LINE_MS - introIn#
            introAlpha# = 1
            if introIn# < introFade# then introAlpha# = introIn# / introFade#
            if introLeft# < introFade# then introAlpha# = introLeft# / introFade#
            color text INTRO_TEXT_ID, rgb(255, 255, 255, 255 * introAlpha#)

            ` the dark comes in with the first line, and goes out with the last one
            introEnd# = introTotal - introAge
            introDim# = 1
            if introAge < INTRO_FADE_MS then introDim# = introAge / introFade#
            if introEnd# < introFade# then introDim# = introEnd# / introFade#
            color sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, rgb(4, 8, 24, INTRO_DIM_ALPHA * introDim#)
        endif

        if new action down(ACT_CONFIRM) then introDone = 1
        introClicked = mouseClickAnywhere() `a click is the confirm key here. see THE MOUSE in fish_headers_mouse.
        if introClicked then introDone = 1

        ` the water goes on being drawn underneath
        gosub update_frame
        sync
    endwhile

    hide sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE
    hide text INTRO_TEXT_ID

    ` the first little board. the hints for moving and swapping are where they always are, along the
    ` bottom, and the one for info mode waits for the end.
    HINT_NO_INFO = 1
    hintShow(1)
    TUTORIAL_GROW_TO = 1
    gosub tutorial_grow
return


` a move has just popped fish on a little board. handle_combos comes here, once for every move that
` does. the words go, and the first pop brings in the moves and the multiplier, with a puff of bubbles.
` the next board waits for the board to settle. see tutorial_advance.
tutorial_pop:
    if TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE then return
    TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE = 1
    tutCaptionNow# = tweenVal(TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TWEEN_ID)
    create basic tween TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TWEEN_ID, tutCaptionNow#, 0, 250, 0
    tutCaptionNow# = tweenVal(TUTORIAL_SUB_TWEEN_ID)
    create basic tween TUTORIAL_SUB_TWEEN_ID, tutCaptionNow#, 0, 250, 0

    if TUTORIAL_STAGE = 2
        gosub tutorial_show_moves
        spawnBubbles(56, 30, 22, 14, 0, rgb(255, 255, 255))
        spawnBubbles(MULT_POS.x + 30, MULT_POS.y + 28, 22, 14, 120, rgb(255, 255, 255))
    endif
return


` the main loop comes here on every frame of the game. once a little board has popped, and the board
` has settled, the next one comes in, or the whole board does. and once info mode has been closed at
` the end of the tutorial, the fish of the mystery comes.
tutorial_advance:
    ` the main loop only comes here while info mode is closed
    if TUTORIAL_STAGE = 6
        gosub tutorial_mystery
        return
    endif

    if TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE = 0 then return
    if REQUEST_COMBO_CHECK then return
    if LIVE_MOVE_ACTIVE then return

    TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE = 0
    gosub clear_queued_moves

    ` the stage is one more than the little board that was just played, so it is the next one
    if TUTORIAL_STAGE < 4
        TUTORIAL_GROW_TO = TUTORIAL_STAGE
        gosub tutorial_grow
    else
        gosub tutorial_finish
    endif
return


` bring in the little board TUTORIAL_GROW_TO. the fish that are on the board now stay where they are
` on the screen, and the new ones grow in around them, a ring at a time. the first board grows in
` from nothing. a fish that is not the one that the new board has in its spot, because the player made
` some other swap than the one that the last board was about, grows in again as the right one.
tutorial_grow:
    tgStep = TUTORIAL_GROW_TO
    tgOldSize = 0
    if TUTORIAL_BOARD then tgOldSize = CELL_COLUMN_COUNT

    ` the fish, and how they face, go with the fish, and the cells are about to be numbered again
    if tgOldSize > 0
        tgOldLast = CELL_COUNT - 1
        for tgI = 0 to tgOldLast
            EXPAND_VALUES(tgI) = CELLS(tgI).value
            TUTORIAL_FACE_KEEP(tgI) = SCHOOL_FACE(tgI)
            TUTORIAL_SHOWN_KEEP#(tgI) = SCHOOL_SHOWN#(tgI)
        next
    endif

    tgSize = tutorialLayoutSize(tgStep)
    tgShift = (tgSize - tgOldSize) / 2
    tutorialGrid(tgSize)

    tgLongest = 0
    tgLast = CELL_COUNT - 1
    for tgI = 0 to tgLast
        tgX = CELLS(tgI).coord.x
        tgY = CELLS(tgI).coord.y
        CELLS(tgI).value = tutorialLayoutKind(tgStep, tgX, tgY)
        CELLS(tgI).comboForce = 0
        CELLS(tgI).comboBlownUp = 0
        clearCellStack(tgI)
        GLOW_TURN#(tgI) = 0
        RAINBOW_FISH(tgI) = 0

        ` a fish that was on the last board is still there, if it is the right one
        tgKept = 0
        tgOldX = tgX - tgShift
        tgOldY = tgY - tgShift
        if tgOldSize > 0
            if tgOldX >= 0 and tgOldX < tgOldSize
                if tgOldY >= 0 and tgOldY < tgOldSize then tgKept = 1
            endif
        endif
        if tgKept
            tgOldI = tgOldX + tgOldY * tgOldSize
            if EXPAND_VALUES(tgOldI) <> CELLS(tgI).value then tgKept = 0
        endif

        if tgKept
            SCHOOL_FACE(tgI) = TUTORIAL_FACE_KEEP(tgOldI)
            SCHOOL_SHOWN#(tgI) = TUTORIAL_SHOWN_KEEP#(tgOldI)
            create basic tween CELLS(tgI).scaleWaveTweenId, 1, 1, 1, 0
        else
            schoolNewFish(tgI)

            ` a new fish grows in with the ring around the board that it is on, going out from the middle.
            ` the rings go one after the other, and the fish of a ring follow each other around it a little.
            tgRingX = tgX - tgSize / 2
            if tgRingX < 0 then tgRingX = 0 - tgRingX
            tgRingY = tgY - tgSize / 2
            if tgRingY < 0 then tgRingY = 0 - tgRingY
            tgRing = tgRingX
            if tgRingY > tgRing then tgRing = tgRingY
            tgDelay = tgRing * TUTORIAL_GROW_STAGGER + (tgX + tgY) * 12
            if tgDelay > tgLongest then tgLongest = tgDelay
            create basic tween CELLS(tgI).scaleWaveTweenId, 0, 1, TUTORIAL_GROW_MS, tgDelay
            size sprite CELLS(tgI).spriteId, 0, 0
            spawnBubbles(getCellX(tgX), getCellY(tgY), CELL_SIZE / 4, 3, tgDelay + 100, FISH_COLORS(getFishColorIndex(CELLS(tgI).value)))
        endif

        updateCell(CELLS(tgI))
        set sprite alpha CELLS(tgI).spriteId, 255
        show sprite CELLS(tgI).spriteId
        hide sprite CELLS(tgI).fxSpriteId
    next

    ` the cursor stays on the fish that it was on. on the first board, it starts in the middle, on the crab.
    if tgOldSize > 0
        SELECTION_POS.x = SELECTION_POS.x + tgShift
        SELECTION_POS.y = SELECTION_POS.y + tgShift
    else
        SELECTION_POS.x = tgSize / 2
        SELECTION_POS.y = tgSize / 2
    endif
    scale sprite SELECTION_SPRITE, CELL_SIZE, CELL_SIZE
    gosub update_selection_position
    cursorArrive(tgLongest + TUTORIAL_GROW_MS) `once the last fish has grown in. see fish_headers_cursorshow.

    TUTORIAL_BOARD = 1
    TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE = 0
    TUTORIAL_STAGE = tgStep + 1

    ` the words of the board. the second board has a line under it too: the cursor moves for free, and
    ` a swap that pops nothing is what costs. a swap like that on the third board brings that line back.
    if tgStep = 1 then set text loc TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID, "intro.tut.swap"
    if tgStep = 2 then set text loc TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID, "intro.tut.free"
    if tgStep = 3 then set text loc TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID, "intro.tut.shape"
    create basic tween TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TWEEN_ID, 0, 1, 400, tgLongest
    create basic tween TUTORIAL_SUB_TWEEN_ID, 0, 0, 1, 0
    if tgStep = 2
        create basic tween TUTORIAL_SUB_TWEEN_ID, 0, 1, 400, tgLongest + 600
    endif

    ` the fish grow in while the game waits. the frame goes on being drawn underneath.
    TUTORIAL_WAIT_UNTIL = game ms() + tgLongest + TUTORIAL_GROW_MS
    gosub tutorial_wait
return


` draw frames until TUTORIAL_WAIT_UNTIL, while something of the tutorial plays out
tutorial_wait:
    while game ms() < TUTORIAL_WAIT_UNTIL
        gosub update_frame
        sync
    endwhile
return


` the fish of the board shrink away, from the middle out, and the game waits for them. the cursor goes
` too. with TUTORIAL_SHRINK_HUD, the things around the board fade away along with them, and are put
` away, which leaves nothing but the water.
tutorial_shrink_board:
    tsLast = CELL_COUNT - 1
    tsLongest = 0
    for tsI = 0 to tsLast
        tsRingX = CELLS(tsI).coord.x - CELL_COLUMN_COUNT / 2
        if tsRingX < 0 then tsRingX = 0 - tsRingX
        tsRingY = CELLS(tsI).coord.y - CELL_ROW_COUNT / 2
        if tsRingY < 0 then tsRingY = 0 - tsRingY
        tsRing = tsRingX
        if tsRingY > tsRing then tsRing = tsRingY
        tsDelay = tsRing * TUTORIAL_GROW_STAGGER
        if tsDelay > tsLongest then tsLongest = tsDelay
        tsFrom# = tweenVal(CELLS(tsI).scaleWaveTweenId)
        create basic tween CELLS(tsI).scaleWaveTweenId, tsFrom#, 0, TUTORIAL_GROW_MS, tsDelay
    next
    hide sprite SELECTION_SPRITE

    tsStart = game ms()
    tsSpan# = tsLongest + TUTORIAL_GROW_MS
    TUTORIAL_WAIT_UNTIL = tsStart + tsLongest + TUTORIAL_GROW_MS
    while game ms() < TUTORIAL_WAIT_UNTIL
        if TUTORIAL_SHRINK_HUD
            tsAge# = game ms() - tsStart
            HUD_KEEP# = 1 - tsAge# / tsSpan#
            if HUD_KEEP# < 0 then HUD_KEEP# = 0
        endif
        gosub update_frame
        sync
    endwhile

    if TUTORIAL_SHRINK_HUD
        gosub tutorial_hide_moves
        gosub tutorial_hide_score
        HUD_KEEP# = 1
    endif
    for tsI = 0 to tsLast
        hide sprite CELLS(tsI).spriteId
    next
return


` the fish of the board grow back, and the things around the board come back, the way they were
` before tutorial_shrink_board took them away
tutorial_regrow_board:
    trLast = CELL_COUNT - 1
    trLongest = 0
    for trI = 0 to trLast
        trDelay = (CELLS(trI).coord.x + CELLS(trI).coord.y) * TUTORIAL_FISH_STAGGER
        if trDelay > trLongest then trLongest = trDelay
        create basic tween CELLS(trI).scaleWaveTweenId, 0, 1, TUTORIAL_FISH_GROW, trDelay
        size sprite CELLS(trI).spriteId, 0, 0
        if CELLS(trI).value > 0
            show sprite CELLS(trI).spriteId
        endif
    next
    cursorArrive(trLongest + TUTORIAL_FISH_GROW)
    gosub tutorial_show_moves
    gosub tutorial_show_score
    applyHudFade() `with HUD_KEEP# at 1, this puts back what the fade took
    hintShow(1)
    TUTORIAL_WAIT_UNTIL = game ms() + trLongest + TUTORIAL_FISH_GROW
    gosub tutorial_wait
return


` the board that the game was dealt comes in, as it was dealt, with the streams of the seed where they
` were, and the moves and the multiplier as a game starts with them. the swaps of the little boards are
` not part of the game. this does not wait for the fish to grow in: TUTORIAL_WAIT_UNTIL says when they have.
tutorial_deal_in:
    resizeGrid(GRID_START_COUNT, GRID_START_COUNT)
    for tdI = 0 to 399
        SCHOOL_FACE(tdI) = TUTORIAL_DEAL_FACE(tdI)
        SCHOOL_SHOWN#(tdI) = 0
    next
    SCHOOL_SPAWNS = TUTORIAL_DEAL_SPAWNS
    for tdI = 0 to 2
        set random stream state tdI, TUTORIAL_RNG(tdI * 2), TUTORIAL_RNG(tdI * 2 + 1)
    next

    ` the fish come in. each one grows from nothing, and the ones at the top left go first, so that
    ` they come in as a wave from that corner. frame_scale_wave is what sizes them.
    tdLast = CELL_COUNT - 1
    tdLongest = 0
    for tdI = 0 to tdLast
        CELLS(tdI).value = TUTORIAL_DEAL(tdI)
        CELLS(tdI).comboForce = 0
        CELLS(tdI).comboBlownUp = 0
        clearCellStack(tdI)
        GLOW_TURN#(tdI) = 0
        RAINBOW_FISH(tdI) = 0
        updateCell(CELLS(tdI))
        set sprite alpha CELLS(tdI).spriteId, 255
        hide sprite CELLS(tdI).fxSpriteId

        tdDelay = (CELLS(tdI).coord.x + CELLS(tdI).coord.y) * TUTORIAL_FISH_STAGGER
        if tdDelay > tdLongest then tdLongest = tdDelay
        create basic tween CELLS(tdI).scaleWaveTweenId, 0, 1, TUTORIAL_FISH_GROW, tdDelay
        size sprite CELLS(tdI).spriteId, 0, 0
        show sprite CELLS(tdI).spriteId
    next

    SELECTION_POS.x = CELL_COLUMN_COUNT / 2
    SELECTION_POS.y = CELL_ROW_COUNT / 2
    scale sprite SELECTION_SPRITE, CELL_SIZE, CELL_SIZE
    gosub update_selection_position
    cursorArrive(tdLongest + TUTORIAL_FISH_GROW)

    CURRENT_MOVE_COUNT = 0
    set text MOVE_COUNT_TEXT_ID, "0"
    resetMultiplier()
    coralTrailClear()
    TUTORIAL_WAIT_UNTIL = game ms() + tdLongest + TUTORIAL_FISH_GROW
return


` the third little board has popped. its fish go, and the things around it, which leaves the water.
` then the line about info mode, and the key to open it. the key brings in the board that the game was
` dealt, with the bar of the round, and info mode opens over it.
tutorial_finish:
    TUTORIAL_BOARD = 0
    create basic tween TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TWEEN_ID, 0, 0, 1, 0
    create basic tween TUTORIAL_SUB_TWEEN_ID, 0, 0, 1, 0

    TUTORIAL_SHRINK_HUD = 1
    gosub tutorial_shrink_board

    ` the line about info mode, over the water, and the hint for it on its own, where it always is.
    ` frame_hints makes it bob after a while.
    TUTORIAL_STAGE = 5
    HINT_NO_INFO = 0
    HINT_ONLY_INFO = 1
    hintShow(1)
    TUTORIAL_KEY_MS = game ms()
    set text loc INTRO_TEXT_ID, "intro.line.info"
    show text INTRO_TEXT_ID
    show sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE
    tfStart = game ms()

    tfEntered = 0
    while tfEntered = 0
        ` the main loop is not running, so this keeps the picture of the key right. it is a
        ` picture of a button if the player picks up a controller.
        gosub frame_input_icons

        tfIn# = game ms() - tfStart
        tfFade# = INTRO_FADE_MS
        tfAlpha# = 1
        if tfIn# < tfFade# then tfAlpha# = tfIn# / tfFade#
        color text INTRO_TEXT_ID, rgb(255, 255, 255, 255 * tfAlpha#)
        color sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, rgb(4, 8, 24, INTRO_DIM_ALPHA * tfAlpha#)

        if new action down(ACT_INFO) then tfEntered = 1

        gosub update_frame
        sync
    endwhile

    hide sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE
    hide text INTRO_TEXT_ID
    TUTORIAL_KEY_MS = 0
    HINT_ONLY_INFO = 0
    hintShow(1)

    ` the board that the game was dealt comes in, with everything around it, and the bar of the round
    ` and the rounds that are left for the first time
    gosub tutorial_deal_in
    gosub tutorial_show_moves
    gosub tutorial_show_score
    applyHudFade() `with HUD_KEEP# at 1, this puts back what the fade took
    spawnBubbles(WORLD_WIDTH / 2, 20, 40, 18, 0, rgb(255, 255, 255))
    spawnBubbles(WORLD_WIDTH - 80, 30, 22, 14, 120, rgb(255, 255, 255))
    gosub tutorial_wait

    ` and info mode opens over the board, which is what the player asked for. the hint to close it
    ` again starts to bob, if it is left open. when it is closed, tutorial_advance brings the fish of
    ` the mystery.
    TUTORIAL_STAGE = 6
    TUTORIAL_INFO_MS = game ms()
    gosub info_open
return


` THE FISH OF THE MYSTERY. info mode has been closed at the end of the tutorial. the board fades away
` to the water, and one seahorse shows a few of the things that can happen to a fish, without saying
` what they are: it turns around, rolls over, shimmers with the rainbow, and swaps out into nothing and
` back, with question marks coming up out of it. "Remember," over it, and "The ocean is mysterious."
` under it. then the line about the game, on a screen of its own, and the board comes back.
tutorial_mystery:
    TUTORIAL_STAGE = 7
    hintShow(0)
    TUTORIAL_SHRINK_HUD = 1
    gosub tutorial_shrink_board

    ` the one fish is in the middle of a little board of its own, with nothing around it
    tutorialGrid(3)
    for tmI = 0 to 8
        CELLS(tmI).value = 0
        CELLS(tmI).comboForce = 0
        CELLS(tmI).comboBlownUp = 0
        clearCellStack(tmI)
        GLOW_TURN#(tmI) = 0
        RAINBOW_FISH(tmI) = 0
        hide sprite CELLS(tmI).spriteId
        hide sprite CELLS(tmI).fxSpriteId
    next
    tmFish = 4
    CELLS(tmFish).value = TEX_BASS `the seahorse
    tmFace = schoolArtFace(TEX_BASS)
    if tmFace = 0 then tmFace = 1
    SCHOOL_FACE(tmFish) = tmFace `the way its picture faces, so that it is not turned around to start with
    SCHOOL_SHOWN#(tmFish) = 0
    updateCell(CELLS(tmFish))
    set sprite alpha CELLS(tmFish).spriteId, 255
    size sprite CELLS(tmFish).spriteId, 0, 0
    show sprite CELLS(tmFish).spriteId
    create basic tween CELLS(tmFish).scaleWaveTweenId, 0, 1, TUTORIAL_FISH_GROW, 0
    SELECTION_POS.x = 1
    SELECTION_POS.y = 1
    scale sprite SELECTION_SPRITE, CELL_SIZE, CELL_SIZE
    gosub update_selection_position
    cursorArrive(TUTORIAL_FISH_GROW)

    ` "Remember," over the fish, and the rest of it under the fish, on the line that is under a
    ` little board. it is white here, and bigger, because it is the point of the whole thing.
    set text loc TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID, "intro.tut.remember"
    create basic tween TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TWEEN_ID, 0, 1, 500, 300
    set text loc TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID, "intro.tut.mysterious"
    size text max TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID, WORLD_WIDTH - 40, 24
    color text TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID, rgb(255, 255, 255, 255)
    create basic tween TUTORIAL_SUB_TWEEN_ID, 0, 1, 500, 1300
    tmNextMark = 700

    ` what the fish does, and when, in milliseconds from when it shows up
    tmMiddleX# = getCellX(1)
    tmLeftX# = getCellX(0)
    tmY = getCellY(1)
    tmSpan# = 0
    tmStart = game ms()
    tmLit = 0
    tmShockLeft = 0
    tmShockRight = 0
    tmShrunk = 0
    tmDone = 0
    while tmDone = 0
        tmAge = game ms() - tmStart

        ` it turns around to face the other way, and back. see WHAT SHOWS in fish_headers_glow.
        tmTurn# = 0
        if tmAge > 900
            if tmAge < 2300
                tmTurnAge# = tmAge - 900
                tmSpan# = 1400
                tmTurn# = sin((tmTurnAge# * 3.14159) / tmSpan#)
            endif
        endif
        GLOW_TURN#(tmFish) = tmTurn#

        ` it rolls over, belly up, and back. see frame_fish_fx.
        tmBelly = 0
        if tmAge > 2600
            if tmAge < 3700 then tmBelly = 1
        endif
        CELLS(tmFish).bellyUp = tmBelly

        ` it shimmers with the rainbow. see fish_headers_rainbow.
        RAINBOW_FISH(tmFish) = 0
        if tmAge > 4300
            if tmAge < 6200 then RAINBOW_FISH(tmFish) = 1
            if tmLit = 0
                tmLit = 1
                RAINBOW_LIT_FROM(tmFish) = game ms()
                RAINBOW_LIT_UNTIL(tmFish) = game ms() + 700
            endif
        endif

        ` and it swaps to the left, into nothing, and back to the right, the way a swap carries a fish
        tmSlide# = 0
        if tmAge > 6600
            tmSlideAge# = tmAge - 6600
            tmSpan# = 220
            tmSlide# = tmSlideAge# / tmSpan#
            if tmShockLeft = 0
                tmShockLeft = 1
                spawnCursorWake(1, 1)
                spawnShockwaveToward(1, 1, -1, 0, SHOCK_SWAP_STRENGTH#, 0, SHOCK_LIFE)
            endif
        endif
        if tmSlide# > 1 then tmSlide# = 1
        if tmAge > 7500
            tmSlideAge# = tmAge - 7500
            tmSpan# = 220
            tmSlide# = 1 - tmSlideAge# / tmSpan#
            if tmSlide# < 0 then tmSlide# = 0
            if tmShockRight = 0
                tmShockRight = 1
                spawnCursorWake(0, 1)
                spawnShockwaveToward(0, 1, 1, 0, SHOCK_SWAP_STRENGTH#, 0, SHOCK_LIFE)
            endif
        endif
        ` it eases into each stop
        tmEase# = tmSlide# * tmSlide# * (3 - 2 * tmSlide#)
        tmX# = tmMiddleX# + (tmLeftX# - tmMiddleX#) * tmEase#
        position sprite CELLS(tmFish).spriteId, tmX#, tmY
        position sprite SELECTION_SPRITE, tmX#, tmY

        ` a question mark comes up out of the fish, now and then, wherever the fish is
        if tmAge > tmNextMark
            if tmAge < 8400
                tmNextMark = tmAge + 650 + rnd(400)
                tmMarkX# = tmX# + rnd(9) - 4
                tmMarkY# = tmY - 6
                tutorialMarkSpawn(tmMarkX#, tmMarkY#)
            endif
        endif
        tutorialMarksStep()

        ` the confirm button goes on to the end
        tmSkip = 0
        if new action down(ACT_CONFIRM) then tmSkip = 1
        tmClicked = mouseClickAnywhere()
        if tmClicked then tmSkip = 1
        if tmSkip
            if tmAge < 9000 then tmStart = game ms() - 9000
        endif

        ` then the words and the fish go
        if tmAge > 9000
            if tmShrunk = 0
                tmShrunk = 1
                tmFrom# = tweenVal(TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TWEEN_ID)
                create basic tween TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TWEEN_ID, tmFrom#, 0, 300, 0
                tmFrom# = tweenVal(TUTORIAL_SUB_TWEEN_ID)
                create basic tween TUTORIAL_SUB_TWEEN_ID, tmFrom#, 0, 300, 0
                create basic tween CELLS(tmFish).scaleWaveTweenId, 1, 0, TUTORIAL_GROW_MS, 0
                hide sprite SELECTION_SPRITE
            endif
        endif
        if tmAge > 9800 then tmDone = 1

        gosub update_frame
        sync
    endwhile

    GLOW_TURN#(tmFish) = 0
    CELLS(tmFish).bellyUp = 0
    CELLS(tmFish).bellyShown# = 0
    RAINBOW_FISH(tmFish) = 0
    RAINBOW_LIT_UNTIL(tmFish) = 0
    hide sprite CELLS(tmFish).spriteId
    tutorialMarksClear()

    ` the line under a little board goes back to the way that the second board has it
    set text loc TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID, "intro.tut.miss"
    size text max TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID, 340, 16
    color text TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID, rgb(255, 230, 150, 255)

    ` then a screen of its own about the game: "You cannot lose.", and how many rounds, under it
    TUTORIAL_LINES_SET = 1
    gosub tutorial_lines

    ` and the board comes back, as it was dealt, with everything around it
    gosub tutorial_deal_in
    gosub tutorial_show_moves
    gosub tutorial_show_score
    applyHudFade() `with HUD_KEEP# at 1, this puts back what the fade took
    hintShow(1)
    gosub tutorial_wait

    ` and what a round is: the bar that fills up
    gosub tutorial_round_bar
    TUTORIAL_STAGE = 0
return


` THE BAR OF THE ROUND. see fish_headers. the water darkens, and the bar, its name and its numbers are
` lifted over the dark, with an outline that pulses around them. the bar fills up once, fizzing at the
` top, and empties out again, while the lines under it say that filling it finishes the round. the
` score is 0 all the while, so the bar only shows what its tween is told. the confirm key moves on.
tutorial_round_bar:
    trbX = SCORE_POS.x - 6
    trbY = SCORE_POS.y - 19
    trbW = SCORE_SIZE.x + 12
    trbH = 39
    layoutInfoBorder(TUTORIAL_BAR_BORDER, trbX, trbY, trbW, trbH)
    set text position TUTORIAL_BAR_TEXT_ID, WORLD_WIDTH / 2, trbY + trbH + 8
    set text position TUTORIAL_BAR_SUB_TEXT_ID, WORLD_WIDTH / 2, trbY + trbH + 32

    ` over the dark, which is at ORDER_INTRO
    order sprite SCORE_BAR.backgroundSpriteId, ORDER_INTRO + 2
    order sprite SCORE_BAR.foregroundSpriteId, ORDER_INTRO + 2
    order text SCORE_BAR.textNumId, ORDER_INTRO + 2
    order text SCORE_BAR.textTitleId, ORDER_INTRO + 2

    color sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, rgb(4, 8, 24, 0)
    show sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE
    show text TUTORIAL_BAR_TEXT_ID
    show text TUTORIAL_BAR_SUB_TEXT_ID
    showInfoBorder(TUTORIAL_BAR_BORDER, 1)
    spawnBubbles(WORLD_WIDTH / 2, SCORE_POS.y, 40, 10, 0, rgb(255, 230, 150))

    TUTORIAL_BAR_DEMO = 1
    trbStart = game ms()
    trbFilled = 0
    trbEmptied = 0
    trbFizz = 0
    trbDone = 0
    trbFade# = 400
    while trbDone = 0
        trbAge = game ms() - trbStart

        ` the bar fills, and empties again
        if trbAge >= TUTORIAL_BAR_FILL_AT
            if trbFilled = 0
                trbFilled = 1
                create basic tween SCORE_BAR.progressTweenId, 0, 1, TUTORIAL_BAR_FILL_MS, 0
            endif
        endif
        if trbAge >= TUTORIAL_BAR_EMPTY_AT
            if trbEmptied = 0
                trbEmptied = 1
                create basic tween SCORE_BAR.progressTweenId, tweenVal(SCORE_BAR.progressTweenId), 0, 500, 0
            endif
        endif

        ` it fizzes while it is full, the way a full bar does in the game
        trbFull = 0
        if trbFilled
            if trbEmptied = 0
                if tweenVal(SCORE_BAR.progressTweenId) >= 1 then trbFull = 1
            endif
        endif
        if trbFull
            if game ms() >= trbFizz
                trbFizz = game ms() + 60
                spawnBubblesOnLayer(SCORE_BAR.pos.x + rnd(SCORE_BAR.size.x), SCORE_BAR.pos.y + 2, 2, 1, 0, rgb(190, 225, 255), ORDER_INTRO + 3, 40, 255, 1)
            endif
        endif

        ` everything fades in, and out at the end
        trbIn# = trbAge
        trbLeft# = TUTORIAL_BAR_MS - trbAge
        trbAlpha# = 1
        if trbIn# < trbFade# then trbAlpha# = trbIn# / trbFade#
        if trbLeft# < trbFade# then trbAlpha# = trbLeft# / trbFade#
        if trbAlpha# < 0 then trbAlpha# = 0
        color sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, rgb(4, 8, 24, INTRO_DIM_ALPHA * 1.6 * trbAlpha#)
        set text alpha TUTORIAL_BAR_TEXT_ID, 255 * trbAlpha#
        trbSubIn# = trbIn# - 500
        trbSubAlpha# = 1
        if trbSubIn# < trbFade# then trbSubAlpha# = trbSubIn# / trbFade#
        if trbSubAlpha# < 0 then trbSubAlpha# = 0
        if trbAlpha# < trbSubAlpha# then trbSubAlpha# = trbAlpha#
        set text alpha TUTORIAL_BAR_SUB_TEXT_ID, 255 * trbSubAlpha#

        ` the outline pulses gently
        trbNow# = game ms()
        trbPulse# = .75 + sin(trbNow# * .006) * .25
        colorInfoBorder(TUTORIAL_BAR_BORDER, rgb(255, 222, 96, 255 * trbAlpha# * trbPulse#))

        ` the confirm key, or a click, goes on: the rest of it fades out
        trbSkip = 0
        if new action down(ACT_CONFIRM) then trbSkip = 1
        trbClicked = mouseClickAnywhere()
        if trbClicked then trbSkip = 1
        if trbSkip
            trbSkipTo = TUTORIAL_BAR_MS - trbFade#
            if trbAge < trbSkipTo then trbStart = game ms() - trbSkipTo
        endif
        if trbAge >= TUTORIAL_BAR_MS then trbDone = 1

        gosub update_frame
        sync
    endwhile

    ` everything back the way it is in the game, with an empty bar
    TUTORIAL_BAR_DEMO = 0
    create basic tween SCORE_BAR.progressTweenId, 0, 0, 1, 0
    order sprite SCORE_BAR.backgroundSpriteId, 0
    order sprite SCORE_BAR.foregroundSpriteId, 0
    order text SCORE_BAR.textNumId, ORDER_HUD_TEXT
    order text SCORE_BAR.textTitleId, ORDER_HUD_TEXT
    hide sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE
    hide text TUTORIAL_BAR_TEXT_ID
    hide text TUTORIAL_BAR_SUB_TEXT_ID
    showInfoBorder(TUTORIAL_BAR_BORDER, 0)
return


` lines of text over the darkened water, one at a time, the way the first lines of the tutorial go. a
` line can have a smaller one under it. TUTORIAL_LINES_SET says which lines: 1 the line about the game
` after the fish of the mystery, 2 the lines before the first upgrade screen. the confirm button goes on
` to the next line.
tutorial_lines:
    tlCount = 3
    if TUTORIAL_LINES_SET = 1 then tlCount = 1
    tlLine = 0
    tlShown = -1
    tlStart = game ms()
    tlMs# = INTRO_LINE_MS
    tlFade# = INTRO_FADE_MS

    color text INTRO_TEXT_ID, rgb(255, 255, 255, 0)
    color sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, rgb(4, 8, 24, 0)
    show sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE
    show text INTRO_TEXT_ID

    while tlLine < tlCount
        if tlLine <> tlShown
            tlShown = tlLine
            tlStart = game ms()
            tlLong = 0 `a line with a smaller one under it stays up for longer
            hide text INTRO_SUB_TEXT_ID
            if TUTORIAL_LINES_SET = 1
                set text loc INTRO_TEXT_ID, "intro.line.nolose"
                set text loc INTRO_SUB_TEXT_ID, "intro.line.rounds", "rounds", GAME_ROUND_CAP
                show text INTRO_SUB_TEXT_ID
                tlLong = 2
            endif
            if TUTORIAL_LINES_SET = 2
                if tlLine = 0 then set text loc INTRO_TEXT_ID, "intro.line.hi"
                if tlLine = 1
                    set text loc INTRO_TEXT_ID, "intro.line.round1"
                    set text loc INTRO_SUB_TEXT_ID, "intro.line.goodjob"
                    show text INTRO_SUB_TEXT_ID
                    tlLong = 1
                endif
                if tlLine = 2 then set text loc INTRO_TEXT_ID, "intro.line.upgrade"
            endif
            tlMs# = INTRO_LINE_MS
            if tlLong = 1 then tlMs# = INTRO_LINE_MS + 800
            if tlLong = 2 then tlMs# = INTRO_LINE_MS + 2000
        endif

        ` every line fades in, stays a while, and fades out
        tlIn# = game ms() - tlStart
        tlLeft# = tlMs# - tlIn#
        tlAlpha# = 1
        if tlIn# < tlFade# then tlAlpha# = tlIn# / tlFade#
        if tlLeft# < tlFade# then tlAlpha# = tlLeft# / tlFade#
        if tlAlpha# < 0 then tlAlpha# = 0
        color text INTRO_TEXT_ID, rgb(255, 255, 255, 255 * tlAlpha#)

        ` the smaller line comes in a little after its line, and goes with it
        tlSubIn# = tlIn# - 600
        tlSubAlpha# = 1
        if tlSubIn# < tlFade# then tlSubAlpha# = tlSubIn# / tlFade#
        if tlAlpha# < tlSubAlpha# then tlSubAlpha# = tlAlpha#
        if tlSubAlpha# < 0 then tlSubAlpha# = 0
        color text INTRO_SUB_TEXT_ID, rgb(255, 230, 150, 255 * tlSubAlpha#)

        ` the dark comes in with the first line, and goes out with the last one
        tlDim# = 1
        if tlLine = 0
            if tlIn# < tlFade# then tlDim# = tlIn# / tlFade#
        endif
        if tlLine = tlCount - 1
            if tlLeft# < tlFade# then tlDim# = tlLeft# / tlFade#
        endif
        if tlDim# < 0 then tlDim# = 0
        color sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE, rgb(4, 8, 24, INTRO_DIM_ALPHA * tlDim#)

        tlNext = 0
        if tlLeft# <= 0 then tlNext = 1
        if new action down(ACT_CONFIRM) then tlNext = 1
        tlClicked = mouseClickAnywhere() `a click is the confirm key here. see THE MOUSE in fish_headers_mouse.
        if tlClicked then tlNext = 1
        if tlNext then tlLine = tlLine + 1

        gosub update_frame
        sync
    endwhile

    hide sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE
    hide text INTRO_TEXT_ID
    hide text INTRO_SUB_TEXT_ID
return


` THE FIRST UPGRADE. the first round of a game that had the tutorial has been won, and the upgrade screen
` is about to come up for the first time. handle_ability_selection comes here first. the board fades away,
` a few lines say what the upgrade screen is, and the board comes back for when it is done. no bubbles
` float up while the lines are up, not even the ones of the full bar, so that there is only the water.
tutorial_upgrade_talk:
    TUTORIAL_UPGRADE_TALK = 0
    hintShow(0)
    TUTORIAL_SHRINK_HUD = 1
    gosub tutorial_shrink_board
    TUTORIAL_QUIET_BUBBLES = 1
    clearBubbles()
    TUTORIAL_LINES_SET = 2
    gosub tutorial_lines
    TUTORIAL_QUIET_BUBBLES = 0
    gosub tutorial_regrow_board
return


` put back everything that a tutorial took away. reset_game comes here, so that a game that is
` started while a tutorial is still going has all of its pieces.
tutorial_end:
    TUTORIAL_SCORE_HOLD = 0
    TUTORIAL_INFO_MS = 0
    TUTORIAL_UPGRADE_TALK = 0
    TUTORIAL_QUIET_BUBBLES = 0
    if TUTORIAL_STAGE = 0 then return
    TUTORIAL_STAGE = 0
    TUTORIAL_BOARD = 0
    TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE = 0

    TUTORIAL_KEY_MS = 0
    HINT_ONLY_INFO = 0
    HINT_NO_INFO = 0
    create basic tween TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TWEEN_ID, 0, 0, 1, 0
    create basic tween TUTORIAL_SUB_TWEEN_ID, 0, 0, 1, 0
    hide text TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID
    hide text TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID
    hide sprite INTRO_DIM_SPRITE
    hide text INTRO_TEXT_ID
    HUD_KEEP# = 1

    ` a little board is put away. reset_game deals the whole board again.
    resizeGrid(GRID_START_COUNT, GRID_START_COUNT)
    scale sprite SELECTION_SPRITE, CELL_SIZE, CELL_SIZE

    for tutI = 0 to CELL_COUNT - 1
        create basic tween CELLS(tutI).scaleWaveTweenId, 1, 1, 1, 0
        show sprite CELLS(tutI).spriteId
    next
    cursorArriveEnd(0)
    show sprite SELECTION_SPRITE
    hintShow(1)

    gosub tutorial_show_moves
    gosub tutorial_show_score
    applyHudFade()
return


` the count of moves, and the multiplier, on the left of the board. info mode does not explain them while they are away.
tutorial_hide_moves:
    hide text MOVES_LABEL_TEXT_ID
    hide text MOVE_COUNT_TEXT_ID
    hide text MULT_LABEL_TEXT_ID
    hide text MULT_TEXT_ID
    hide text MULT_NUM_TEXT_ID
    hide sprite MULT_BAR_BACK_SPRITE
    hide sprite MULT_BAR_FILL_SPRITE
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_MOVE_COUNT, 0)
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_MULTIPLIER, 0)
return

tutorial_show_moves:
    show text MOVES_LABEL_TEXT_ID
    show text MOVE_COUNT_TEXT_ID
    show text MULT_LABEL_TEXT_ID
    show text MULT_TEXT_ID
    show text MULT_NUM_TEXT_ID
    show sprite MULT_BAR_BACK_SPRITE
    show sprite MULT_BAR_FILL_SPRITE
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_MOVE_COUNT, 1)
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_MULTIPLIER, 1)
return


` the bar of the round's progress, above the board, and the rounds that are left, on the right of it
tutorial_hide_score:
    hide sprite SCORE_BAR.backgroundSpriteId
    hide sprite SCORE_BAR.foregroundSpriteId
    hide sprite OVERFLOW_SPRITE
    hide text SCORE_BAR.textNumId
    hide text SCORE_BAR.textTitleId
    hide text ROUNDS_LABEL_TEXT_ID
    hide text ROUND_COUNT_TEXT_ID
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_SCORE_BAR, 0)
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_ROUNDS, 0)
return

tutorial_show_score:
    show sprite SCORE_BAR.backgroundSpriteId
    show sprite SCORE_BAR.foregroundSpriteId
    show sprite OVERFLOW_SPRITE
    show text SCORE_BAR.textNumId
    show text SCORE_BAR.textTitleId
    show text ROUNDS_LABEL_TEXT_ID
    show text ROUND_COUNT_TEXT_ID
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_SCORE_BAR, 1)
    setInfoBlobEnabled(INFO_INDEX_ROUNDS, 1)
return


` lay out the three key hints of the game, and shake the one that is about what the player just did.
` update_frame comes here on every frame of the game. see THE HINTS, at the top of this file.
frame_hints:

    ` a direction on its own is a move, and a direction while the swap button is held is a swap
    hintDir = 0
    if new action down(ACT_LEFT) then hintDir = 1
    if new action down(ACT_RIGHT) then hintDir = 1
    if new action down(ACT_UP) then hintDir = 1
    if new action down(ACT_DOWN) then hintDir = 1
    if hintDir
        if action down(ACT_SWAP)
            create basic tween HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(1), 1, 0, HINT_SHAKE_MS, 0
        else
            create basic tween HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(0), 1, 0, HINT_SHAKE_MS, 0
        endif
    endif
    if new action down(ACT_INFO)
        create basic tween HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(2), 1, 0, HINT_SHAKE_MS, 0
    endif

    ` the pictures of keys in the words of the tutorial jump when their key is pressed, the swap
    ` button on its own, and the direction whether or not the swap button is held
    hintIconHit0 = new action down(ACT_SWAP)
    hintIconHit2 = new action down(ACT_INFO)
    if hintIconHit0
        iconPunch(0)
    endif
    if hintDir
        iconPunch(1)
    endif
    if hintIconHit2
        iconPunch(2)
    endif
    for hintIconI = 0 to 2
        hintIconScale# = 1 + tweenVal(ICON_PUNCH_TWEENS(hintIconI)) * ICON_PUNCH_SIZE#
        set text icon scale TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID, ICON_PUNCH_IDS(hintIconI), hintIconScale#
        set text icon scale INTRO_TEXT_ID, ICON_PUNCH_IDS(hintIconI), hintIconScale#
    next

    ` they sit in a row, in the middle of the screen. the pictures of the keys are not the same width
    ` as the pictures of the controller buttons, so the row is measured again on every frame.
    hintWidth0# = get text size x(HINT_PART_TEXTS(0))
    hintWidth1# = get text size x(HINT_PART_TEXTS(1))
    hintWidth2# = get text size x(HINT_PART_TEXTS(2))
    hintRow# = hintWidth0# + hintWidth1# + hintWidth2# + HINT_PART_GAP * 2
    hintHalf# = hintRow# / 2
    hintX# = WORLD_WIDTH / 2 - hintHalf#

    ` a shake dies away, and the hint ends up back where it started
    hintWave# = sin(game ms() * .07) * HINT_SHAKE_SIZE#

    set text position HINT_PART_TEXTS(0), hintX# + hintWave# * tweenVal(HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(0)), WORLD_HEIGHT - 2
    hintX# = hintX# + hintWidth0# + HINT_PART_GAP
    set text position HINT_PART_TEXTS(1), hintX# + hintWave# * tweenVal(HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(1)), WORLD_HEIGHT - 2
    hintX# = hintX# + hintWidth1# + HINT_PART_GAP

    ` in the very first game, the hint for info mode is on its own to start with. if the player has
    ` not pressed the key after a while, the hint bobs: up a little and back down to where it sits,
    ` gently. it starts from where it sits, so it does not jump.
    hintKeyBob = 0
    if TUTORIAL_KEY_MS > 0
        hintKeyWait# = game ms() - TUTORIAL_KEY_MS
        if hintKeyWait# > TUTORIAL_NUDGE_MS
            hintKeyAge# = hintKeyWait# - TUTORIAL_NUDGE_MS
            hintKeyBob = (cos(hintKeyAge# * TUTORIAL_NUDGE_SPEED#) - 1) * TUTORIAL_NUDGE_SIZE
        endif
    endif

    ` a - b + c comes out as a - (b + c), so the subtraction goes last
    set text position HINT_PART_TEXTS(2), hintX# + hintWave# * tweenVal(HINT_SHAKE_TWEENS(2)), WORLD_HEIGHT + hintKeyBob - 2

    ` the words over a little board sit just above its top row. see THE LITTLE BOARDS, at the top of this file.
    hintCaption# = tweenVal(TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TWEEN_ID)
    if hintCaption# > 0
        hintCaptionY = GRID_POS.y - CELL_SIZE / 2
        set text position TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID, GRID_CENTER.x, hintCaptionY - 8
        set text alpha TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID, hintCaption# * 255
        show text TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID
    else
        hide text TUTORIAL_CAPTION_TEXT_ID
    endif

    ` and the line about a swap that pops nothing sits just under its bottom row
    hintSub# = tweenVal(TUTORIAL_SUB_TWEEN_ID)
    if hintSub# > 0
        hintSubY = GRID_POS.y + (CELL_ROW_COUNT - 1) * CELL_SIZE + CELL_SIZE / 2
        set text position TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID, GRID_CENTER.x, hintSubY + 4
        set text alpha TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID, hintSub# * 255
        show text TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID
    else
        hide text TUTORIAL_SUB_TEXT_ID
    endif

    ` in the very first game, info mode opened by itself, and the only hint is the one to close it.
    ` if it has been left open for a while, that hint bobs the same way, to ask for the key.
    if TUTORIAL_INFO_MS > 0
        hintBob = 0
        if INFO_MODE = 0
            TUTORIAL_INFO_MS = 0
        else
            hintWaited# = game ms() - TUTORIAL_INFO_MS
            if hintWaited# > TUTORIAL_INFO_NUDGE_MS
                hintBobAge# = hintWaited# - TUTORIAL_INFO_NUDGE_MS
                hintBob = (cos(hintBobAge# * TUTORIAL_NUDGE_SPEED#) - 1) * TUTORIAL_NUDGE_SIZE
            endif
        endif

        ` a - b + c comes out as a - (b + c), so the subtraction goes last
        set text position INFO_HINT_TEXT_ID, WORLD_WIDTH / 2, WORLD_HEIGHT + hintBob - 2
    endif
return


routines_intro_exit:


` say if the hints along the bottom are the three of the game (1), or if some other screen has
` written its own hints on INFO_HINT_TEXT_ID (0)
function hintMode(isGame)
    HINT_GAME_ON = isGame
    applyHints()
endfunction


` make a picture of a key in the words of the tutorial jump: 0 is {swap}, 1 is {dir}, and 2 is {info}.
` it grows and comes back, the same way the cursor punches. see ICON_PUNCH_TWEENS in fish_headers.
function iconPunch(punchWhich)
    create basic tween ICON_PUNCH_TWEENS(punchWhich), 0, 1, ICON_PUNCH_MS, 0
    set tween type ICON_PUNCH_TWEENS(punchWhich), 1
endfunction


` put all of the hints away (0), or bring them back (1)
function hintShow(isVisible)
    HINT_VISIBLE = isVisible
    if isVisible
        show text INFO_HINT_TEXT_ID
    else
        hide text INFO_HINT_TEXT_ID
    endif
    applyHints()
endfunction


` the three key hints of the game are only there while the hints are showing, and the game is what
` they are for. this only decides where each one is headed. stepHintFade() takes it there.
function applyHints()
    for hintI = 0 to 2
        show text HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI) `one that has faded all the way out is hidden again by stepHintFade()
    next
endfunction


` how see-through one of the three key hints of the game should be right now, out of 255
function hintPartWant(part)
    want = 0
    if HINT_VISIBLE
        if HINT_GAME_ON then want = HINT_PART_SHOWN_ALPHA
    endif

    ` the hint for info mode on its own, at the start of the very first game. it is bright, to be seen.
    if HINT_ONLY_INFO
        if want > 0
            want = 0
            if part = 2 then want = 255
        endif
    endif

    ` and while the little boards are played, it is the one that is left out
    if HINT_NO_INFO
        if part = 2 then want = 0
    endif
endfunction want


` fade the three key hints of the game toward where they should be. updateSeabed() calls this, which
` is called wherever frames are being drawn, so the hints fade under the menus and the upgrade screen too.
` it works out how much time has gone by on its own, so calling it twice on a frame does no harm.
function stepHintFade()
    fadeNow = game ms()
    fadeElapsed# = fadeNow - HINT_FADE_LAST_MS
    HINT_FADE_LAST_MS = fadeNow
    if fadeElapsed# > 50 then fadeElapsed# = 50
    if fadeElapsed# <= 0 then exitfunction

    ` the texts are not made until setup_intro has run
    if HINT_PART_TEXTS(0) = 0 then exitfunction

    fadeStep# = (fadeElapsed# * 255) / HINT_FADE_MS#

    for hintI = 0 to 2
        want# = hintPartWant(hintI)
        alpha# = HINT_PART_ALPHA#(hintI)
        if alpha# < want#
            alpha# = alpha# + fadeStep#
            if alpha# > want# then alpha# = want#
        endif
        if alpha# > want#
            alpha# = alpha# - fadeStep#
            if alpha# < want# then alpha# = want#
        endif
        HINT_PART_ALPHA#(hintI) = alpha#

        set text alpha HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI), alpha#
        if alpha# <= 0
            hide text HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI)
        else
            show text HINT_PART_TEXTS(hintI)
        endif
    next
endfunction


` THE LITTLE BOARDS. see the top of this file.

` how many cells there are across a little board, and down it. 0 for one that there is not.
function tutorialLayoutSize(tlsStep)
    tlsSize = 0
    if tlsStep = 1 then tlsSize = 3
    if tlsStep = 2 then tlsSize = 5
    if tlsStep = 3 then tlsSize = 7
endfunction tlsSize


` the kind of fish that a little board has in a cell. every row is a number, one digit for every cell,
` and a digit is a kind of fish from TUTORIAL_KINDS:
`     1 puffer, 2 catfish, 3 goldfish, 4 angelfish, 5 crab, 6 seahorse, 7 starfish
` the letters next to the rows say the same: P F G A C S W.
` a board has no group of three to start with. on the second board, only the swap that the board is
` about makes one. the fish that drop in after its pop are the ones that the next board has
` there. fish_tests_tutorial checks all of that.
function tutorialLayoutKind(tlkStep, tlkX, tlkY)
    tlkRow = 0

    ` the seahorses: swap the crab down. the cursor starts on the crab.
    if tlkStep = 1
        if tlkY = 0 then tlkRow = 314 `G P A
        if tlkY = 1 then tlkRow = 656 `S C S
        if tlkY = 2 then tlkRow = 762 `W S F
    endif

    ` the angelfish, along the top: swap the seahorse at the top right with the angelfish at the end.
    ` the cursor comes from the crab of the last board, near the bottom. no other swap pops anything.
    if tlkStep = 2
        if tlkY = 0 then tlkRow = 14464 `P A A S A
        if tlkY = 1 then tlkRow = 65235 `S C F G C
        if tlkY = 2 then tlkRow = 23147 `F G P A W
        if tlkY = 3 then tlkRow = 47521 `A W C F P
        if tlkY = 4 then tlkRow = 16374 `P S G W A
    endif

    ` the angelfish again, down the left side: swap the angelfish on the left edge down, beside the
    ` one to its right, and the four of them make an L. a few other swaps near it pop too, which is fine.
    if tlkStep = 3
        if tlkY = 0 then tlkRow = 3523542 `G C F G C A F
        if tlkY = 1 then tlkRow = 2147167 `F P A W P S W
        if tlkY = 2 then tlkRow = 7652351 `W S C F G C P
        if tlkY = 3 then tlkRow = 4231472 `A F G P A W F
        if tlkY = 4 then tlkRow = 5475216 `C A W C F P S
        if tlkY = 5 then tlkRow = 4163743 `A P S G W A G
        if tlkY = 6 then tlkRow = 4352165 `A G C F P S C
    endif

    ` the digit of the cell. the first cell of a row is the first digit.
    tlkPlace = tutorialLayoutSize(tlkStep) - 1
    tlkPlace = tlkPlace - tlkX
    while tlkPlace > 0
        tlkRow = tlkRow / 10
        tlkPlace = tlkPlace - 1
    endwhile
    tlkDigit = tlkRow mod 10

    tlkKind = 0
    if tlkDigit > 0 then tlkKind = TUTORIAL_KINDS(tlkDigit)
endfunction tlkKind


` the cell of the swap that a little board is about, as a number on that board. `tscEnd` is 0 for
` the fish that the cursor is meant to start the swap on, and 1 for the one that it goes to.
function tutorialSwapCell(tscStep, tscEnd)
    tscX = 0
    tscY = 0
    if tscStep = 1
        tscX = 1
        tscY = 1 + tscEnd
    endif
    if tscStep = 2
        tscX = 4 - tscEnd
        tscY = 0
    endif
    if tscStep = 3
        tscX = 0
        tscY = 3 + tscEnd
    endif
    tscCell = tscX + tscY * tutorialLayoutSize(tscStep)
endfunction tscCell


` make the board a little board, `tgSize` cells across and down. resizeGrid would make its cells big,
` to fill the square of the screen that the board has. a little board keeps the cells the size that
` they are on the board that a game starts with instead, so that it sits in the middle of where that
` board will be, and every cell of it is in the spot of a cell of that board.
function tutorialGrid(tgSize)
    resizeGrid(tgSize, tgSize)
    CELL_SIZE = CELL_START_SIZE
    CELL_ART_SIZE = CELL_START_ART_SIZE

    ` a - b + c comes out as a - (b + c), so the subtraction goes last
    GRID_POS.x = GRID_CENTER.x + CELL_SIZE / 2 - (tgSize * CELL_SIZE) / 2
    GRID_POS.y = GRID_CENTER.y + CELL_SIZE / 2 - (tgSize * CELL_SIZE) / 2

    ` the smoke of a pop is the size that it is on that board too
    tgLast = CELL_MAX_COUNT - 1
    for tgFx = 0 to tgLast
        scale sprite CELLS(tgFx).fxSpriteId, 1, 1
    next

    ` info mode explains the board, wherever the board is now
    coralPlaceInfo()
endfunction


` the kind of the new fish that drops into a cell of a little board, after a pop. it is the fish that
` the next board has in that spot. the last board makes way for the whole board, so any fish that does
` not pop will do there. this does not roll the streams of the seed.
function tutorialNewFish(tnfCell)
    tnfNext = TUTORIAL_STAGE `one more than the little board that is being played
    tnfNextSize = tutorialLayoutSize(tnfNext)
    tnfKind = 0
    if tnfNextSize > 0
        tnfShift = (tnfNextSize - CELL_COLUMN_COUNT) / 2
        tnfX = (tnfCell mod CELL_COLUMN_COUNT) + tnfShift
        tnfY = (tnfCell / CELL_COLUMN_COUNT) + tnfShift
        tnfKind = tutorialLayoutKind(tnfNext, tnfX, tnfY)
    else
        ` the kinds are tried in turn, starting from a different one in every cell. a cell only touches
        ` four others, so one of the seven is always free.
        tnfTry = 0
        while tnfTry < 7
            tnfPick = TUTORIAL_KINDS(((tnfCell + tnfTry) mod 7) + 1)
            tnfGroup = countFishGroup(tnfCell, tnfPick, 2)
            if tnfGroup < 2
                tnfKind = tnfPick
                tnfTry = 7
            endif
            tnfTry = tnfTry + 1
        endwhile
        if tnfKind = 0 then tnfKind = TUTORIAL_KINDS(1)
    endif
endfunction tnfKind


` 1 when a swap between these two cells is not allowed on a little board, and the cursor shakes its
` head. any swap is allowed, but none once the board has popped, until the next board is in, so
` that nothing changes under the board as it grows. startLiveMove asks this about every swap.
function tutorialBlocksSwap(tbsA, tbsB)
    tbsBlocked = 0
    if TUTORIAL_BOARD
        if TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE then tbsBlocked = 1
    endif
    if tbsBlocked
        cursorShakeNo()
    endif
endfunction tbsBlocked


` a swap on a little board popped nothing, and that cost the multiplier. judgeMultiplierSwaps comes here.
` the line under the board says so, and the bar of the multiplier wiggles, so that the player looks at it.
function tutorialMissed()
    if TUTORIAL_BOARD = 0 then exitfunction
    if TUTORIAL_STEP_DONE then exitfunction
    tmsFrom# = tweenVal(TUTORIAL_SUB_TWEEN_ID)
    create basic tween TUTORIAL_SUB_TWEEN_ID, tmsFrom#, 1, 250, 0
    wiggleMultiplierBar()
endfunction


` THE QUESTION MARKS. one more question mark shows up at this spot, and drifts up from it. see THE FISH
` OF THE MYSTERY. they are only for show, so where they go is rolled with rnd.
function tutorialMarkSpawn(tmkX#, tmkY#)
    tmkI = TUTORIAL_MARK_NEXT
    TUTORIAL_MARK_NEXT = (TUTORIAL_MARK_NEXT + 1) mod TUTORIAL_MARK_COUNT
    TUTORIAL_MARK_BORN(tmkI) = game ms()
    TUTORIAL_MARK_X#(tmkI) = tmkX#
    TUTORIAL_MARK_Y#(tmkI) = tmkY#
    size text y TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(tmkI), 12 + rnd(3) * 4
    show text TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(tmkI)
endfunction


` move every question mark that is up along: it drifts up, sways, fades in, and fades away at the end
function tutorialMarksStep()
    tmsNow = game ms()
    tmsLife# = TUTORIAL_MARK_LIFE
    for tmsI = 0 to TUTORIAL_MARK_COUNT - 1
        if TUTORIAL_MARK_BORN(tmsI) > 0
            tmsAge# = tmsNow - TUTORIAL_MARK_BORN(tmsI)
            if tmsAge# >= tmsLife#
                TUTORIAL_MARK_BORN(tmsI) = 0
                hide text TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(tmsI)
            else
                tmsT# = tmsAge# / tmsLife#
                tmsAlpha# = 1
                if tmsT# < .2 then tmsAlpha# = tmsT# / .2
                if tmsT# > .6 then tmsAlpha# = (1 - tmsT#) / .4
                tmsX# = TUTORIAL_MARK_X#(tmsI) + sin(tmsAge# * .004 + tmsI) * TUTORIAL_MARK_SWAY
                tmsY# = TUTORIAL_MARK_Y#(tmsI) - tmsT# * TUTORIAL_MARK_RISE
                set text position TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(tmsI), tmsX#, tmsY#
                set text alpha TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(tmsI), 220 * tmsAlpha#
            endif
        endif
    next
endfunction


` put every question mark away
function tutorialMarksClear()
    for tmcI = 0 to TUTORIAL_MARK_COUNT - 1
        TUTORIAL_MARK_BORN(tmcI) = 0
        hide text TUTORIAL_MARK_TEXTS(tmcI)
    next
endfunction
